    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d667">

                <pb facs="0895" n="793" sameAs="frus:frus1935v01/pg793"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">765.84/1553: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Bingham</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Extract]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1935-10-04T12:00:00+01:00">October 4,
                            1935—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received October 4—8:50 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>492. All press this morning report military operations in Abyssinia noting
                    Italian claims of “preventative police action” and no formal declaration of
                    war.</p>
                <p>I have already asked the Foreign Office whether in the view of His Majesty’s
                    Government a state of war exists between Italy and Abyssinia and am awaiting
                    reply.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . . . . . . . . .</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bingham</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
